// Per-request syscall mix on the request path, which now has no hand-off to hide it.
//
// The profile after the preparation hop was removed still shows `crng_make_state` (getrandom) at
// ~2% and `pvclock_clocksource_read` (a clock read, and on this hypervisor there is no vDSO for it
// -- Phase 5 measured `clock_gettime` as a syscall) at ~3.5%. At a 45 us front-end those are not
// rounding errors, and both are things a server chooses to do per request rather than costs of the
// transport.
//
// Counted rather than inferred: a profile share is a fraction of samples, a count is a fact.
tracepoint:syscalls:sys_enter_getrandom { @gr = count(); }
tracepoint:syscalls:sys_enter_clock_gettime { @cg = count(); }
tracepoint:syscalls:sys_enter_epoll_wait { @ep = count(); }
tracepoint:syscalls:sys_enter_futex { @fx = count(); }
tracepoint:syscalls:sys_enter_writev { @wv = count(); }
tracepoint:syscalls:sys_enter_sendto { @st = count(); }
tracepoint:syscalls:sys_enter_recvfrom { @rf = count(); }
